# Two peers on a DTN. For the first minute both radios' receivers flip about one bit in a thousand (noise 8: eight bits
# per thousand bytes, so a 49-byte call is damaged one time in three). A damaged wire fails its tag and is dropped:
# nothing corrupt ever reaches product code, and a damaged call is a call that did not arrive, which the ttl handles.
# After the minute the noise stops and every call lands.
seed 37
peers 2
profile dtn
0      noise 0 8
0      noise 1 8
60000  noise 0 0
60000  noise 1 0
